/// \defgroup grp_wwlib_thirdparty WWLib and third-party libraries
/// \brief Westwood's WWLib and the third-party code linked into `game.dat`
///        (compression codecs, Lua, STLport, ATL and GDI+, BYTEmark,
///        Microsoft runtime pieces), plus the clean-room VP6 decoder.
///
/// None of this code holds game rules. WWLib supplies files and the file
/// factories, chunked asset I/O, Westwood INI and registry access, strings,
/// containers, CRCs, threads and CPU detection. Most third-party code is
/// reproduced at a recorded upstream release and is documented upstream.
/// \ref sub_wwlib_thirdparty describes the subsystem, how the rest of the
/// engine reaches it and its differences from Zero Hour.
